---
import Section from './ui/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from './ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import ExternalLink from './ui/ExternalLink.astro';
import { currentEvent, nextEventWindow } from '../data/events';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { longDate } from '../lib/format';
---

<Section width="wide">
  <SectionHeading title="About OZ ORC" />
  <div class="two-col">
    <p>
      OZ ORC is a day of the finest in old-school D&D and OSR gaming. We've dug
      up TTRPGs from throughout the OSR scene, from weird-punk sci-fi
      post-apocalypse to classic D&D and original-edition Dungeons & Dragons.
      We've gathered together a dozen of Adelaide's most experienced and capable
      GMs to take you through worlds of exploration, treasure, and death.
    </p>
    <p>
      No matter if you are the most grizzled grognard or you're entirely new to
      the hobby, we will have a game that will fill you with awe and terror.
    </p>
    {
      currentEvent ? (
        <p>
          Join us on {longDate(currentEvent.date)} at the{' '}
          {currentEvent.venue.name} for a day of adventure like nothing you've
          ever seen before, at Adelaide's Premier old-school gaming convention!
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Our next convention is planned for {nextEventWindow}. Join the{' '}
          <a href="#register" class="link">
            mailing list
          </a>{' '}
          to hear first when the date and games are announced.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p>
      We've started OZ ORC as a chance to bring the old-school and its glories
      to everyone in Adelaide. Everyone is welcome to bring dice, snacks, and
      their wits with them and test themselves against the dangers of the
      deepest delves. Read our <a href="/code-of-conduct/" class="link"
        >Code of Conduct</a
      > to learn more about our commitment to creating a welcoming environment.
    </p>
    <figure class="illo">
      {
        /* The sizes values are the rendered widths: one column below 760px, half
           the two-column text above it, capped at 526px. Change them with the
           layout, or phones fetch a bigger file than they need. */
      }
      <img
        src="/images/gallery/sep-2026/wrap-up-01.webp"
        srcset="/images/gallery/sep-2026/wrap-up-01-480w.webp 480w, /images/gallery/sep-2026/wrap-up-01-720w.webp 720w, /images/gallery/sep-2026/wrap-up-01.webp 960w"
        sizes="(min-width: 760px) min(50vw - 50px, 526px), calc(100vw - 54px)"
        alt="Wide view of the hall at OZ ORC, with players at tables between partition screens"
        width="959"
        height="722"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="label-caps">
        <span>Fig. 1</span> The hall at a past OZ ORC.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ExternalLink
      href={currentEvent?.warhornUrl || site.socials.discord}
      class="btn btn-primary btn-lg"
    >
      {currentEvent?.warhornUrl ? 'Register Now' : 'Join our Discord'}
      <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </ExternalLink>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  /* Two-column module text with a drop cap. */
  .two-col p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  .two-col p:first-of-type::first-letter {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    float: left;
    font-size: 3.6em;
    line-height: 0.9;
    padding: 0.04em 0.1em 0 0;
  }

  .illo {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border: var(--border) solid var(--color-rule);
    background-color: var(--surface-raised);
    break-inside: avoid;
  }

  .illo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .illo figcaption {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    border-top: var(--border) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .illo figcaption span {
    background-color: var(--color-spot);
    color: var(--color-spot-content);
    padding: 0 0.35rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .two-col {
      column-count: 2;
      column-gap: 2.5rem;
      column-rule: var(--border) solid var(--color-rule);
    }
  }
</style>
